@* Where it runs, on the Architecture page: Docker on a developer's machine or a customer's own, and this site in Azure. *@
<Band Id="where-it-runs" Kicker="where it runs">
    <h3>Docker on your own hardware, or Container Apps in Azure.</h3>
    <div class="grid-2">
        <article class="panel">
            <h4>On a developer's machine</h4>
            <p>Every host is a Docker image on the .NET SDK, started from a demo's compose file with the repository mounted as the workspace. Rider starts the ACP server per chat, the API serves the web app on one port, and a local model runs in Ollama beside them when a profile asks for it.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="panel">
            <h4>In Azure, from GitHub</h4>
            <p>This site is one Container App in Azure's South African region, its own image with its guide and nothing else, asleep when nobody visits. Its keys sit in a vault, and a merge to <code>main</code> releases it after green CI, signed in without a password. A customer's site with an agent runs the same way, or on the customer's own hardware.</p>
        </article>
    </div>
</Band>
